# Strings are “...“ byte blocks. U turns one into a list of char codes, so every
# list op works on strings; O prints a byte block, J prints a code list.  That
# "every list op" now includes the polymorphic + - * ⌈ ⌊, so a Caesar shift is
# an addition: the shape of the operands already says to do it once per letter.
“Hello, world!“O10)      # puts a literal                 -> Hello, world!
“stressed“UVJ10)          # reverse, via chars->rev->join  -> desserts
“Hello“U1+J10)            # +1 on every character code     -> Ifmmp
